It sounds awesome, but the distance and my (lack of) money forbids me
to go this year.

I don't know what the usual topics are, but this year's jbonunsla
could be a good place to begin some debates about the potential
upcoming trawl of la gimste. Is there universal agreement that a look-
through is in order? How is it best accomplished - by having people
report weird definitions to the BPFK when they encounter them, or is
any systematic search through la gimste preferable?

Just a fun idea off the top of my head: Making sandwitches in pairs
where one part is blindfolded and must put the sandwitches together
with help from instructions given in Lojban by the other part.
Perhaps some sort of geocashing (orienteering?) where the instructions
on how to complete the run is given in Lojban.
Or speed-authoring, where a group of people each have a set amount of
time to write the beginning of a short story. Then after 5-10 minutes,
the paper it's written on is given to the person to the left, which
continues the story. The game ends when everyone has written part of
every story.

Have a good jbonunsla, doi ro salci

